{"t": 1794119201.2837198, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "*[checkout] PaymentGatewayErrors (AG-7731) \u2014 root cause + fix*\n\n*What was wrong:* Gateway 4xx rate hit 38% because checkout was sending euro decimals in the charge payload. Loki shows: `WARN gateway rejected charge status=400 body={\"error\":\"invalid_amount\",\"message\":\"amount must be an integer in minor units (cents), got 12.34\"}` followed by `INFO gateway api version switched to 2026-11 (strict amounts)` at 07:41 UTC. Gateway API 2026-11 now requires `amount` as an integer in minor units (cents); `checkout/gateway.py` was passing `amount_eur` (float euros) straight through, so every charge was rejected.\n\n*Fix:* `checkout/gateway.py::charge_payload` now converts euros to integer cents (Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP) before building the payload: `{\"amount\": 1234, \"currency\": \"EUR\"}`. Verified locally for 12.34 / 0.01 / 19.99 / 100.00 (1234 / 1 / 1999 / 10000). No other checkout call sites in the repo.\n\n*Next:* deploy the fix, watch gateway 4xx rate for checkout, then resolve AG-7731. No rounding policy or API schema docs were found in Confluence/Notion/repo; the contract used is the one stated in the gateway error body (integer cents).", "channel_id_placeholder": ""}, "ok": true}
